  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "A nucleus splits into two nuclear parts which have their velocity ratio equal to $2: 1 .$ What will be the ratio of their nuclear radius?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "IcTJ6",
      "text": "$2^{1 / 3}: 1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lFHsO",
      "text": "$1: 2^{1 / 3}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "2PYJU",
      "text": "$3^{1 / 2}: 1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "oaGNZ",
      "text": "$1: 3^{1 / 2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As momentum is conserved, therefore\r\n\r\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{m}_{1}}{\\mathrm{~m}_{2}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{A}_{1}}{\\mathrm{~A}_{2}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{v}_{2}}{\\mathrm{v}_{1}}=\\frac{1}{2}$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\frac{\\mathrm{R}_{1}}{\\mathrm{R}_{2}}=\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{A}_{1}}{\\mathrm{~A}_{2}}\\right)^{1 / 3}=\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{1 / 3}=1: 2^{1 / 3}$",
    "image": null
  },
